      "id": "r2",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "97. Is he a Chandala ( pariah ) or a Bràhmana ( twice-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "born ), is he a Súdra or an ascetic, or is he some great saint,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "whose intellect is acute enough to understand philosophical",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "truths: ascetics, although thus spoken of by people, garrulcus",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "on account of the doubts rising within them, quietly (or, self-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "delighted) go their way neither offended nor pleased at heart.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "98. The creator ordained the air to serve the serpents as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "food—not involving the sin of destroying life, and accessible",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "without any effort; animals living on land he made to eat",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "grass; (but) to men, whose talents are capable of bearing",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "them over the ocean of life, he has assigned such a living",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "that while in pursuit of it all their good qualities are inva-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "riably brought to an end ( exhausted ).",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "99. Can those blessed days be ( in store ) for me, when",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "I, having fixed myself in the Padmâsana posture on a slab in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the Himàlayas on the bank of the Ganges, and having gone",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "to the sleep of concentration while in the act of constantly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "contemplating Bràhman, the old stags (growing) fearless",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "will rub their bodies against mine ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "100. Those blessed ones–whose hand is ( to them ) a clean",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "pot, and alms acquired by wandering ( an ) inexhaus-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "tible ( supply of ) food, to whom the extensive ten quarters",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "are as a spotless garment, and the earth as a spacious bed,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "whose development is in accepting renunciation, who are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "contented with themselves, and who have got rid of a num-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "ber of opportunities of humiliation—root out Karma.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "101. O mother, earth; O father, wind; O friend, light;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "O water, my good relation, and O brother, sky; here do",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "I fold, for the last time, my palms in salutation to you; by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "means of pure knowledge resulting from the preponderance",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of merit accumulated by virtue of association with you, all",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "the trammels of infatuation having been removed, I now",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "merge in the Supreme Brahman.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
